label start:

    scene black

    pause 2.0

    p_j_d "{w=1.0}My letters hadn't gone through. {w=2.0}He hasn't written back."
    p_j_d "{w=1.0}...Lord, I've sinned against you. Please be merciful to me. {w=1.0}Please. {w=1.0}I don't deserve it, but..."
    g_s "BARK!"
    p_j_d "-!"
    g_s "BARK!{w=0.5} BARK!"
    p_j_d "..."
    n "He bends down and leaves bread for the dog, which he laps up."

    pause 1.0
    p_j_d "'Even the dogs eat the crumbs from under their master's table.' {w=0.5}...even the dogs...'"

    pause 1.0

    jump chapter_1

label chapter_1:

    scene bg bedroom

    pause 3.0

    j "-!"
    j "'Forgive me, Lord! {w=0.5}I'll pray at the table!'"
    n "The first words Joey utters before he gets up...{w=0.5}really every morning. {w=0.5}Farmers chuckle as he throws on his sweater, and hops down the hall, slipping on his loafers."
    
    scene bg kitchen

    with fade

    pause 1.0

    n "As he stumbles into the kitchen, a can of chickpeas rolls out-"
    
    pause 1.0

    show Jenkin Neutral at left
 
    je "Dawgone it! {w=0.5}No place for the beans. {w=0.5}Boys, no steak tonight! {w=0.5}We're eating stew!"
    
    show Joey Uneasy at right

    pause 1.0

    n "He turns, watching Joey fix his collar."

    show Jenkin Angry at left:
        xzoom -1

    pause 1.0

    n "You woke up late again!"

    pause 1.0

    je "Joey, you live here, too. Your job is to get up and take the sheep to graze! What are you doin at night?! EH?!"
    
    pause 1.0

    j "I was praying the other night."

    hide Jenkin Angry
    show Jenkin Neutral at left:
        xzoom -1

    pause 2.0

    je "Fine. {w=0.5}Do it earlier.{w=0.5} You got no other reason to stay up.{w=0.5} Got it?"
    j "Yes sir."

    pause 1.0

    show Jenkin Gentle at left:
        xzoom -1

    je "Boy, I'm no pastor.{w=0.5} It's Jenkins, Ted even."
    je "Heh,{w=0.5} if your bold, you can call me Teddy."

    pause 1.0
    hide Joey Uneasy
    show Joey Gentle at right
   
    n "Joey huffs out a chuckle, taking the plate."

    hide Joey Gentle
    hide Jenkin Gentle

    menu:
        "Sausage":
            $ after_food = "Sausage"
            jump Sausage
        "Eggs":
            $ after_food = "Eggs"
            jump Eggs
        "Toast":
            $ after_food = "Toast"
            jump Toast

label Sausage:

    scene bg sausage
    with fade

    play music ""

    n "The sausage was spiraled up, {w=0.5}charred from a black burn from the pan."
    
    pause 2.0

    scene bg sausage flashback

    with fade

    n "He cooked the sausage, the scent of grease rising, the popping of oil rising up. Every pop seared onto his wrists and arms as the sausage curled like a cobra, until-{w=2.0}"
    n "POP!"
    n "Joey screamed, dropping down, pan falling as he Dad rushed in."
    n "He bandages his wound, wrapping it hard around his wrist."
    j "Dad, it hurts!"
    j_d "I don't care."
    j "Dad!"
    j_d "BE QUIET! BE QUIET!!!"
    pause 3.0
    j "..."
    j_d "He pulled out a brown sweater. Though the air was hot, the sleeves covered Joey's wounds."
    j_d "Take it off, tear it, get so much as a stain, and I'll give you something to cry about!"
    j_d "Fail that test of yours, and your wearing it all summer! Got it?!"
    j "{w=0.2}Yes."
    j_d "...Go to the library."
    j "Ok"
    pause 1.0
    j_d "I love you."
    pause 2.0
    j "I-love-you-too."
    
    pause 1.0

    n "Joey steps out, his Dad trails behind him and takes a seat outside the porch, watching him. Joey hangs his head, walking to the library."
    n "Sweat oozed from his head, and he wiped it furiously, lest the collar become soaked."

    jump after_story

label Eggs:

    scene eggs

    with fade

    n "The eggs were fluffy, {w=0.5}just like a chicken's butt."
    
    pause 2.0

    scene eggs flashback

    with fade

    n "...Joey was taken outside. His head hung low like an anvil hanging from a thread."
    j_d "'I'm trash? I'm trash?! TAKE YOUR SHOE OFF!'"
    
    pause 1.0

    n "THWACK"
    j "Augh!"
    j_d "-!"
    n "Joey clutched his head, blood flowing down."

    pause 1.0

    n "As the sun set, the boy stared at the mirror, watching tuffs of brown fall down ss he held his head. He got to hold the mirror."
    j "I look like a chicken."
    j_d "Heh. A chickens butt."
    j "...You hit me."
    j_d "I paid for those shoes, so Imma remind you I did."
    j_d "Say that again, and I'll get your next pair from the dumpster."
    j_d "Got it?"
    j "Yes."
    j_d "Good. {w=3.0}Heh, you got chicken legs."
    n "Joey looks down, seeing his shoes are on the wrong feet. He doesn't move. His Dad does fixes them for him."
    j_d "Can't do anything, huh? Heh, chickens are as chickens do..."

    jump after_story

label Toast:

    scene bg toast

    with fade

